    "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nTurns on `automatic_shard` for four steps, and for the AMD mirrors of three of them. They were previously going to be split by hand (#58781, #58775, #58777, #58000), but automatic sharding replaces that approach. Only the flag changes; no commands or tests change.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Each step runs as parallel jobs planned from main's per-file timings, and each job runs only its share of the tests:\n\n| Step | Command shape | Planned shards |\n|---|---|---:|\n| `language-models-test-mteb` (optional) | one `pytest` over a directory | 3 |\n| `amd-language-models-test-mteb` (optional mirror) | same | 2 |\n| `amd-spec-decode-dflash-nightly` (optional mirror) | same as its step | 1 for now (see Details) |\n| `spec-decode-dflash-nightly` (optional) | `pytest` over a directory with `-k`; the large test file is split by test | 3 |\n| `moe-refactor-integration-test-b200-dp-temporary` (optional) | `pytest` on one eval file with `--config-list-file`, split by test | 3 |\n| `entrypoints-integration-llm` | `export` setup, then three `pytest` commands with `--ignore` | 3 |\n| `amd-entrypoints-integration-llm` (mirror) | same as its step | 2 |\n\n- Every test runs exactly once across the shards, with the same environment as the single job.\n- If planning fails, the step falls back to running as one job, as it does today.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Planned each step on this branch with ci-infra main's `runtime_shard.plan_step`, using main's timings on the step's own queue.\n- Rendered each step with the pipeline generator and ran every shard's commands against a mock test tree, as a PR build and with main's `pytest -p ci_otel` wrapper. Every test of every command ran in exactly one shard, with the same env.\n- `/ci run` exercises `entrypoints-integration-llm` and its AMD mirror. The other three steps and their mirrors are optional, so a PR build doesn't run them; they need a build scoped to their keys.\n\n## Details\n\n- **Left out on purpose.** Some steps from the hand-split PRs aren't in this batch:\n  - `pytorch-fullgraph-test` runs each file in its own pytest process; sharding would put them in one process and could change results.\n  - `multi-modal-models-standard-4-other-whisper` runs one command from the repo root (`cd ..`), which the planner can't split.\n  - `hybrid-ssm-nixlconnector-pd-accuracy-tests-4-gpus` runs a bash script, not pytest.\n  - `lm-eval-humming-*-act` steps have no per-file timings on main.\n  - `multi-modal-models-extended-generation-1` currently fails on main, so a sharded run can't be compared against a passing baseline.\n- **AMD mirrors.** Every mirror that runs longer than 20 minutes as one job is enrolled: MTEB, DFlash Nightly and Entrypoints (LLM). DFlash's mirror moved to another AMD queue on main (#61955) after it was validated here (2 shards, both passed). That queue has no per-file timings for it yet, so it runs as one job, as it does today, well inside its 120-minute timeout. It starts sharding once nightly runs there record timings. MoE Refactor's mirror runs in a few minutes, so it stays one job.\n- **Where to look.** The `automatic_shard: true` lines in `.buildkite/test_areas/{models_language,spec_decode,lm_eval,entrypoints}.yaml`.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>** (anything written below this line will be removed by GitHub Actions)\n",
